endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 201 0 R
/T (The increasing use of interconnected cameras,meters, controllers and environmental sensors creates a need to organize security observations across many devices. Isolated login failures or unusual telemetry values provide limited context when a simulated intrusion progresses through several hosts. HoneyGraph is a MongoDB-native threat-intelligence and attack-chain reconstruction engine that addresses this problem through validated event storage, database-driven detection and linked evidence. The project operates entirely on software-generated traffic and does not execute exploits or interact with real IoT devices. )
/E (The increasing use of interconnected cameras,meters, controllers and environmental sensors creates a need to organize security observations across many devices. Isolated login failures or unusual telemetry values provide limited context when a simulated intrusion progresses through several hosts. HoneyGraph is a MongoDB-native threat-intelligence and attack-chain reconstruction engine that addresses this problem through validated event storage, database-driven detection and linked evidence. The project operates entirely on software-generated traffic and does not execute exploits or interact with real IoT devices. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 201 0 R
/T (The proposed system combines a three-member MongoDB replica set, a Python FastAPI backend and a React dashboard. Events are retained in a regular collection and protected by per-device SHA-256 hash chains. Detection rules are stored as aggregation pipelines and refreshed through change streams. Alerts are correlated using bounded graph traversal; incidents, alert links and device risk scores are persisted within a multi-document transaction. Time-series telemetry rollups, geospatial searches, role-based access control and an authenticated WebSocket feed support operational investigation. )
/E (The proposed system combines a three-member MongoDB replica set, a Python FastAPI backend and a React dashboard. Events are retained in a regular collection and protected by per-device SHA-256 hash chains. Detection rules are stored as aggregation pipelines and refreshed through change streams. Alerts are correlated using bounded graph traversal; incidents, alert links and device risk scores are persisted within a multi-document transaction. Time-series telemetry rollups, geospatial searches, role-based access control and an authenticated WebSocket feed support operational investigation. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 201 0 R
/T (The principal contribution is the use of MongoDB features to connect collection design with observable defensive behavior. The implementation demonstrates runtime rule changes, ordered lateral-movement evidence, decaying risk and exact first-link tamper diagnostics. Historical verification records include a 100,000-event integrity check and a browser-based end-to-end flow. The system provides a practical DBMS learning platform while making explicit the limits of local performance measurements, retained evidence, failover durability and external integrity anchors. )
/E (The principal contribution is the use of MongoDB features to connect collection design with observable defensive behavior. The implementation demonstrates runtime rule changes, ordered lateral-movement evidence, decaying risk and exact first-link tamper diagnostics. Historical verification records include a 100,000-event integrity check and a browser-based end-to-end flow. The system provides a practical DBMS learning platform while making explicit the limits of local performance measurements, retained evidence, failover durability and external integrity anchors. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
