/T (Performance is evaluated separately for database bulk insertion, indexed retrieval, detector latency and integrity checking. The saved benchmark corpus contains one million records per ingestion mode; direct-insert rates are not equivalent to HTTP API throughput. The historical browser gate measured 304 ms live alert delivery. These observations describe the tested environment rather than a guaranteed service-level objective. )
/E (Performance is evaluated separately for database bulk insertion, indexed retrieval, detector latency and integrity checking. The saved benchmark corpus contains one million records per ingestion mode; direct-insert rates are not equivalent to HTTP API throughput. The historical browser gate measured 304 ms live alert delivery. These observations describe the tested environment rather than a guaranteed service-level objective. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
434 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 206 0 R
/T (Consistency requires incident creation or update, alert linkage and risk upsert in one transaction using snapshot reads and majority writes. Ingestion batches use a transaction with w:1 and restore cached heads after failure. This prevents partial batch chains, while w:1 can still lose a recent acknowledged write during primary failure before replication. )
/E (Consistency requires incident creation or update, alert linkage and risk upsert in one transaction using snapshot reads and majority writes. Ingestion batches use a transaction with w:1 and restore cached heads after failure. This prevents partial batch chains, while w:1 can still lose a recent acknowledged write during primary failure before replication. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
435 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 206 0 R
/T (Security requires password hashing, JWT validation, service-specific MongoDB privileges and recursive rule checks. Reliability requires resume-token persistence and clear invalid-request handling. Maintainability is supported by typed modules and tests. Usability requires loading, empty and error states, socket status and role- aware navigation. The local Compose deployment uses HTTP; production TLS is an extension rather than an implemented property. )
/E (Security requires password hashing, JWT validation, service-specific MongoDB privileges and recursive rule checks. Reliability requires resume-token persistence and clear invalid-request handling. Maintainability is supported by typed modules and tests. Usability requires loading, empty and error states, socket status and role- aware navigation. The local Compose deployment uses HTTP; production TLS is an extension rather than an implemented property. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
