/T (An event depends on its ObjectId and device sequence; a rule depends on ruleId; an application user depends on username. Unique indexes enforce business keys. Alerts retain stage and severity from the triggering rule so past detections remain interpretable after edits. Incident chains duplicate selected alert values for efficient readback. Controlled copies trade storage and refresh responsibility for simpler investigation reads. )
