/T (HoneyGraph demonstrates how a DBMS project cancombine structured evidence storage with defensive investigation. Collection boundaries reflect differing lifetimes and access patterns of inventory, observations, rules and incidents. MongoDB validation, unique indexes and typed requests constrain critical records while allowing protocol-specific payloads. Software simulation makes the workflow repeatable without physical devices or offensive tooling. )
/E (HoneyGraph demonstrates how a DBMS project cancombine structured evidence storage with defensive investigation. Collection boundaries reflect differing lifetimes and access patterns of inventory, observations, rules and incidents. MongoDB validation, unique indexes and typed requests constrain critical records while allowing protocol-specific payloads. Software simulation makes the workflow repeatable without physical devices or offensive tooling. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
643 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 217 0 R
/T (The implementation integrates change-stream detection, runtime aggregation rules, graph correlation and transaction-backed incident materialization. Per-device hash chains provide tamper evidence without a global ordering bottleneck. Separate time-series rollups preserve the regular events collection needed for change streams. The dashboard connects these database functions to alert inspection, ordered evidence, geospatial risk and integrity demonstrations. )
/E (The implementation integrates change-stream detection, runtime aggregation rules, graph correlation and transaction-backed incident materialization. Per-device hash chains provide tamper evidence without a global ordering bottleneck. Separate time-series rollups preserve the regular events collection needed for change streams. The dashboard connects these database functions to alert inspection, ordered evidence, geospatial risk and integrity demonstrations. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
644 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 217 0 R
/T (Verification supports these behaviors with explicit limits. The Phase 9 record documents 304 ms live delivery, runtime rule creation, ordered four-hop evidence, role restrictions and status history. Saved bulk benchmarks report 33,251.4 events/s without chaining and 19,592.4 events/s with chaining using direct writes in an isolated corpus, not the validated HTTP path. Perfect reported quality scores come from a simplified evaluator with false positives fixed at zero; the failover script checks post-election ingestion rather than proving no alert loss. Stronger independent validation is needed before broader claims are made. )
/E (Verification supports these behaviors with explicit limits. The Phase 9 record documents 304 ms live delivery, runtime rule creation, ordered four-hop evidence, role restrictions and status history. Saved bulk benchmarks report 33,251.4 events/s without chaining and 19,592.4 events/s with chaining using direct writes in an isolated corpus, not the validated HTTP path. Perfect reported quality scores come from a simplified evaluator with false positives fixed at zero; the failover script checks post-election ingestion rather than proving no alert loss. Stronger independent validation is needed before broader claims are made. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
