/P 217 0 R
/T (Future work should coordinate heads across backend workers, schedule correlation and telemetry explicitly, test recovery under sustained failover traffic and evaluate quality with labeled normal as well as malicious traces. Production use also requires TLS, secret rotation, evidence archival and externally protected anchors. Within its course scope, HoneyGraph provides an inspectable foundation for studying document modelling, aggregation, indexing, transactions, replication and defensive-security data flows. )
/E (Future work should coordinate heads across backend workers, schedule correlation and telemetry explicitly, test recovery under sustained failover traffic and evaluate quality with labeled normal as well as malicious traces. Production use also requires TLS, secret rotation, evidence archival and externally protected anchors. Within its course scope, HoneyGraph provides an inspectable foundation for studying document modelling, aggregation, indexing, transactions, replication and defensive-security data flows. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [10]
>>
