1586 0 obj
<<
/Title (The increasing use of interconnected cameras,meters, controllers and environmental sensors creates a need to organize security observations across many devices. Isolated login failures or unusual telemetry values provide limited context when a simulated intrusion progresses through several hosts. HoneyGraph is a MongoDB-native threat-intelligence and attack-chain reconstruction engine that addresses this problem through validated event storage, database-driven detection and linked evidence. The project operates entirely on software-generated traffic and does not execute exploits or interact with real IoT devices.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1575 0 R
/Next 1599 0 R
>>
endobj
1587 0 obj
<<
/Title (The principal contribution is the use of MongoDB features to connect collection design with observable defensive behavior. The implementation demonstrates runtime rule changes, ordered lateral-movement evidence, decaying risk and exact first-link tamper diagnostics. Historical verification records include a 100,000-event integrity check and a browser-based end-to-end flow. The system provides a practical DBMS learning platform while making explicit the limits of local performance measurements, retained evidence, failover durability and external integrity anchors.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1575 0 R
/Prev 1599 0 R
>>
endobj
