/Last 1620 0 R
/Count -3
>>
endobj
1605 0 obj
<<
/Title (HoneyGraph demonstrates how a DBMS project cancombine structured evidence storage with defensive investigation. Collection boundaries reflect differing lifetimes and access patterns of inventory, observations, rules and incidents. MongoDB validation, unique indexes and typed requests constrain critical records while allowing protocol-specific payloads. Software simulation makes the workflow repeatable without physical devices or offensive tooling.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1590 0 R
/Next 1621 0 R
>>
endobj
1606 0 obj
<<
/Title (Future work should coordinate heads across backend workers, schedule correlation and telemetry explicitly, test recovery under sustained failover traffic and evaluate quality with labeled normal as well as malicious traces. Production use also requires TLS, secret rotation, evidence archival and externally protected anchors. Within its course scope, HoneyGraph provides an inspectable foundation for studying document modelling, aggregation, indexing, transactions, replication and defensive-security data flows.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
